Z||000013||JohnnyK||01-04-2001||02:03 AM||||I'll give you a hood for free, as long as you pay for the shipping.||||reg||1
Z||000014||tgowens||01-04-2001||03:29 AM||||Josh, we, at the Fiero Shop in Richmond, CA have hoods for Fieros too. I think I can speak for Bob at Kick Hill as well as Ed Parks, Bob Steiger and several others who deal in Fiero parts - first of all, Pontiac does not make a Fiero hood any longer and therefore it is impossible to get a "new" hood. We buy hoods at junk yards only if they are in good condition - this means that there are no cracks or chips on them - they may need to be repainted due to the fact that these cars are between 12 and 16 years old. The paint simply doesn't last - so, if you intend to buy a "new" hood you are simply out of luck - if you are willing to buy a "used" hood then there are several reputable shops that can supply you with one. <P>All of us have to face the fact, sooner or later, that the parts supply for the Fiero is dwindling. New parts from GM are being discontinued all the time and it is basically because of the shops like ours, and Ed's and Bob's, that there <I>is</I> still an availability for most of the parts required to restore a Fiero. And, where do you think our parts cars come from? Yep, that's right, some come from "junk-yards"! Others are bought at auctions and from private owners. But - they are all "used" with "used" parts......<P>That's just <I>my</I> 2 cents.......||||reg||1
Z||000015||tgowens||01-04-2001||03:30 AM||||by the way - we have the left headlight doors too.......||||reg||1
